// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — Level 3 (2001–3000字) Unit 1
window.T1_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"aboard – chilly","cards":[{"w":"aboard","p":"prep.","d":"on or onto a ship, aircraft, train, or bus","c":"在（船、飛機、車）上；登上","s":"Before the international flight took off for London, all passengers were asked to show their boarding passes and step aboard the airplane.","t":"在飛往倫敦的國際航班起飛之前，所有乘客都被要求出示登機證並登上飛機。"},{"w":"aboard","p":"adv.","d":"on or into a vehicle","c":"在船（車、飛機）上；上車（船）","s":"The ship was about to leave the harbor, so the tourists quickly climbed aboard to begin their vacation.","t":"船隻即將離開港口，因此遊客們迅速爬上船開始他們的假期。"},{"w":"welcome aboard","p":"phr.","d":"a greeting welcoming someone to a team, ship, or company","c":"歡迎加入；歡迎搭乘","s":"On my very first day at the technology company, the manager shook my hand warmly and said, \"Welcome aboard, we are glad to have you on our team!\"","t":"在我到這家科技公司上班的第一天，經理熱情地和我握手並說：「歡迎加入，我們很高興你成為我們團隊的一員！」"},{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to offer suggestions or recommendations about what to do [advise, advised, advised]","c":"建議；勸告（動詞）","s":"Because the weather forecast predicted heavy rain tomorrow, our experienced teacher advised all of us to bring an umbrella and a warm raincoat.","t":"因為天氣預報預測明天會下大雨，我們經驗豐富的老師建議我們所有人帶一把雨傘和一件保暖雨衣。"},{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to formally inform or notify someone of a fact [advise, advised, advised]","c":"正式通知；告知","s":"The airline agent promised to advise passengers of any schedule changes as soon as the storm passed.","t":"航空公司地勤人員承諾，一旦暴風雨過去，就會立即正式告知乘客任何班次變動。"},{"w":"advice","p":"n.","d":"guidance or recommendations offered regarding choices (uncountable)","c":"建議；忠告（不可數名詞）","s":"Whenever Mark faces difficult choices about his future career, he always visits his parents because they give him very sensible and helpful advice.","t":"每當馬克面臨關於未來職業的艱難抉擇時，他總是去拜訪父母，因為他們會給他非常明智且有用的建議。"},{"w":"adviser","p":"n.","d":"an expert who gives formal advice in a specific area","c":"顧問；指導老師","s":"During his college years in the United States, Jason regularly met with his academic adviser to discuss his graduation requirements and course schedule.","t":"在美國就讀大學期間，傑森定期與他的學業指導顧問會面，討論他的畢業學分要求和課程表。"},{"w":"advise against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to recommend that someone avoid a particular action","c":"建議不要做…；勸阻…","s":"The doctor decided to advise against eating raw seafood because it could easily cause severe stomach problems during the long journey.","t":"醫生決定建議不要吃生海鮮，因為在漫長的旅途中這很容易引起嚴重的腸胃問題。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the assembled spectators or listeners at a public performance","c":"觀眾；聽眾（集合名詞）","s":"After the young pianist finished her marvelous performance on stage, the entire audience stood up and clapped their hands enthusiastically.","t":"在年輕的女鋼琴家於舞台上結束她精彩的演奏後，全體觀眾起立並熱烈鼓掌。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"a formal meeting with a monarch, pope, or other ruler","c":"（正式的）晉見；接見","s":"The foreign ambassador was extremely honored to have a private audience with the king at the royal palace.","t":"外交大使非常榮幸能在皇宮獲得國王的私下面對面接見。"},{"w":"basement","p":"n.","d":"the floor of a building that is partly or entirely below ground","c":"地下室；地庫","s":"During the heavy summer thunderstorm, water began to leak through the wall and accumulated quickly on the floor of our basement.","t":"在猛烈的夏季雷陣雨期間，水開始穿透牆壁滲漏，並迅速積聚在我們地下室的地板上。"},{"w":"bay","p":"n.","d":"a broad inlet of the sea where the land curves inward","c":"海灣","s":"On sunny weekend mornings, many local residents enjoy jogging along the sandy shore of the bay and watching the boats sail.","t":"在陽光明媚的週末早晨，許多當地居民喜歡沿著海灣的沙灘慢跑，欣賞船隻航行。"},{"w":"bay","p":"v.","d":"to bark or howl with a deep, loud voice (esp. wolves/hounds) [bay, bayed, bayed]","c":"（獵犬或狼）吠叫；長嗥","s":"As the silver full moon rose high in the dark night sky, the hungry wolves began to bay loudly in the woods.","t":"當銀色滿月高高升起在黑夜的天空中，飢餓的狼群開始在樹林裡大聲長嗥。"},{"w":"keep at bay","p":"v.phr.","d":"to prevent someone or something dangerous from approaching","c":"使…無法靠近；牽制；遏阻","s":"Eating a balanced diet and exercising regularly can help you keep at bay many common illnesses during the cold winter season.","t":"均衡飲食和規律運動可以幫助你在寒冷的冬季牽制／遏阻許多常見疾病。"},{"w":"beast","p":"n.","d":"a large, wild, or dangerous four-footed animal","c":"野獸；獸類","s":"In the ancient fairy tale, brave villagers traveled deep into the dark mountain forest to hunt the dangerous and terrifying beast.","t":"在那則古老的童話故事中，勇敢的村民們深入黑暗的山林，去獵捕那隻危險而可怕的野獸。"},{"w":"beast","p":"n.","d":"an extraordinarily difficult, formidable, or powerful thing/person","c":"難對付的事物；厲害強者（俚語）","s":"Preparing for the national medical entrance exam is a whole different beast, demanding endless months of intense discipline.","t":"準備全國醫學院入學考試完全是另一回事（極具挑戰性的艱難任務），需要長達數月的高度自律。"},{"w":"canyon","p":"n.","d":"a deep valley with steep rock sides, carved by a river","c":"峽谷","s":"From the high lookout tower, the tourists admired the breathtaking scenery of the deep canyon carved by the rushing river below.","t":"從高處的觀景台，遊客們讚嘆下方湍急河流所切割出的深邃峽谷的壯麗景色。"},{"w":"carpenter","p":"n.","d":"a skilled craftsperson who builds and repairs wooden objects","c":"木工；木匠","s":"Because the old wooden dining table was badly broken, my father hired a skilled carpenter to repair it and make four matching chairs.","t":"因為舊的木製餐桌損壞嚴重，我父親聘請了一位技藝精湛的木工來修理它並製作四張配套的椅子。"},{"w":"chill","p":"v.","d":"to cool food or drink down, or to become pleasantly cold [chill, chilled, chilled]","c":"使冷卻；冷藏；變涼","s":"Before our guests arrive for dinner tonight, please chill the white wine in the refrigerator so that it will taste refreshing.","t":"在今晚我們的客人抵達用餐之前，請先將白酒放進冰箱冷卻，這樣喝起來才會清爽。"},{"w":"chill","p":"n.","d":"an unpleasant sensation of coldness in the air or body","c":"寒意；著涼；寒顫","s":"As the cold northern wind began to blow through the open window, I suddenly felt an unpleasant chill on my skin.","t":"當寒冷的北風開始透過開著的窗戶吹進來時，我突然感到皮膚上一陣難受的寒意。"},{"w":"chill out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to relax completely and calm down from stress or anger","c":"放鬆；冷靜下來","s":"After working hard on the difficult project all week, Susan just wanted to stay home and chill out on the couch.","t":"在辛苦處理了一整週的棘手專案後，蘇珊只想待在家裡並在沙發上好好放鬆。"},{"w":"chilly","p":"adj.","d":"noticeably and uncomfortably cold (of weather) [chilly, chillier, chilliest]","c":"寒冷的；冷颼颼的","s":"Even though the morning sunshine looked bright and inviting, the autumn air was quite chilly outside, so remember to wear a jacket.","t":"雖然早晨的陽光看起來明亮誘人，但戶外的秋天天氣相當寒冷，所以記得穿上一件夾克。"},{"w":"chilly","p":"adj.","d":"unfriendly or cold in manner or reception","c":"冷淡的；不友善的","s":"When the uninvited visitor suddenly walked into the private meeting, he received a very chilly reception from the company directors.","t":"當那位不速之客突然走進私人會議時，他遭到了公司董事們非常冷淡的對待與回應。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"chin – explorer","cards":[{"w":"chin","p":"n.","d":"the bottom part of a person's face below the mouth","c":"下巴；頦","s":"While listening thoughtfully to the lecture, the university student rested his chin on his hand and took detailed notes.","t":"在全神貫注聆聽演講時，那名大學生用手托著下巴並寫下詳細的筆記。"},{"w":"double chin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a fold of thick fatty skin below someone's chin","c":"雙下巴","s":"After gaining weight during the long winter vacation, David noticed that he had developed an obvious double chin in photos.","t":"在漫長的寒假期間體重增加之後，大衛在照片中注意到自己出現了明顯的雙下巴。"},{"w":"keep one's chin up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay cheerful and brave in a difficult or discouraging situation","c":"保持樂觀；不氣餒；振作起來","s":"Even though Mark failed his driver's license exam yesterday, his encouraging parents told him to keep his chin up and try again.","t":"雖然馬克昨天駕照考試沒及格，但他給予鼓勵的父母告訴他要振作起來／保持樂觀，再試一次。"},{"w":"cleaner","p":"n.","d":"a person employed to clean buildings, offices, or houses","c":"清潔人員；清潔工","s":"Early every morning before the office workers arrive, the dedicated cleaner sweeps the hallway floors and empties all the trash bins.","t":"每天清晨在辦公室員工抵達之前，那位盡責的清潔工都會清掃走廊地板並倒空所有垃圾桶。"},{"w":"cleaner","p":"n.","d":"a substance or chemical product used for cleaning things","c":"清潔劑；清潔劑產品","s":"My mother prefers to buy an eco-friendly cleaner because it cleans oily kitchen stoves effectively without harming the environment.","t":"我母親偏好購買環保清潔劑，因為它能有效清除廚房瓦斯爐的油污，又不會傷害環境。"},{"w":"clean","p":"v.","d":"to make something free from dirt or stains by washing or wiping","c":"打掃；清理；洗淨","s":"Before our relatives arrived from out of town for the weekend, we had to clean the entire apartment thoroughly.","t":"在我們的親戚從外地抵達過週末之前，我們必須將整間公寓徹底打掃乾淨。"},{"w":"crispy","p":"adj.","d":"pleasantly thin, dry, and crunchy in a pleasant way","c":"酥脆的；脆生生的","s":"The chef fried the chicken wings at a high temperature so that the skin was golden and crispy while the meat stayed juicy.","t":"主廚用高溫油炸雞翅，使外皮呈現金黃酥脆，而肉質依然鮮嫩多汁。"},{"w":"cruel","p":"adj.","d":"extremely unkind and causing pain or suffering to others intentionally","c":"殘忍的；殘酷的","s":"It is completely unacceptable to be cruel to domestic animals, and anyone who abuses pets should be punished by the law.","t":"對家養動物殘忍是完全不可接受的，任何虐待寵物的人都應當受到法律制裁。"},{"w":"cruelty","p":"n.","d":"cruel behavior or actions that cause pain or distress to others","c":"殘忍行為；殘酷（不可數）","s":"Many animal welfare organizations work tirelessly every day to protect innocent wild animals from human cruelty and exploitation.","t":"許多動物福利組織每天不知疲倦地工作，以保護無辜的野生動物免受人類的殘忍行為與剝削。"},{"w":"database","p":"n.","d":"an organized set of data or information stored electronically in a computer","c":"資料庫","s":"The hospital established a secure national database that stores medical records of thousands of patients for quick doctor access.","t":"這家醫院建立了一個安全的國家資料庫，存放數千名病人的病歷，以便醫師能迅速查閱。"},{"w":"dawn","p":"n.","d":"the first appearance of light in the sky before sunrise","c":"黎明；破曉；拂曉","s":"Hardworking local fishermen usually wake up at dawn to prepare their heavy nets and depart before the morning sun appears.","t":"辛勤的當地漁民通常在黎明時分起床準備沉重的漁網，並在早晨太陽出現之前出海。"},{"w":"dawn","p":"v.","d":"to begin to grow light as the sun rises, or to begin to become evident","c":"破曉；開始展開；萌芽","s":"As the morning finally dawned over the quiet valley, bright golden sunlight illuminated the misty peaks of the high mountains.","t":"當清晨終於在寂靜的山谷中破曉展開時，明亮的金黃陽光照亮了高山多霧的峰頂。"},{"w":"dawn on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become understood or realized by someone for the first time","c":"使某人恍然大悟；某人突然明白","s":"It suddenly dawned on Peter that he had left his apartment keys and wallet inside the locked office downtown.","t":"彼得突然恍然大悟／明白過來，自己把公寓鑰匙和皮夾遺忘在市中心上鎖的辦公室裡了。"},{"w":"dusk","p":"n.","d":"the time at the end of the day just before it becomes completely dark","c":"薄暮；黃昏；傍晚","s":"Streetlights across the busy avenue turn on automatically at dusk so drivers can see pedestrians clearly on their way home.","t":"繁忙大道上的路燈在黃昏時分會自動開啟，以便駕駛人在下班回家的路上能清楚看見行人。"},{"w":"deck","p":"n.","d":"a flat, open floor on a ship, boat, or outdoor platform of a house","c":"甲板；（屋外的）木質露天平台","s":"During the pleasant cruise across the Mediterranean, passengers gathered on the open deck to enjoy the cool evening sea breeze.","t":"在橫跨地中海的心曠神怡遊輪航程中，乘客們聚集在露天甲板上享受涼爽的傍晚海風。"},{"w":"a deck of cards","p":"n.phr.","d":"a full pack of 52 playing cards used in games and magic tricks","c":"一副撲克牌","s":"The talented young magician asked an audience member to choose a single card from a deck of cards and remember its symbol.","t":"那位才華洋溢的年輕魔術師請一位現場觀眾從一副撲克牌中選出一張牌並記住其花色花樣。"},{"w":"deck out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decorate or dress someone or something in a very attractive or festive way","c":"盛裝打扮；裝飾一新","s":"Every December, our neighbors deck out their front garden with colorful glowing lights, plastic reindeer, and holiday wreaths.","t":"每年十二月，我們的鄰居都會用五彩繽紛的發光燈飾、塑膠馴鹿與節慶花環將前院花園裝飾一新。"},{"w":"elderly","p":"adj.","d":"polite term describing people who are old and past middle age","c":"年長的；上了年紀的（客氣說法）","s":"The polite junior high student stood up and offered his comfortable bus seat to an elderly passenger carrying heavy bags.","t":"那位有禮貌的國中生站起身來，將舒適的公車座位讓給一位手提沉重提袋的年長乘客。"},{"w":"the elderly","p":"n.phr.","d":"older people considered as a collective group (used with plural verb)","c":"年長者；銀髮族；長輩（複數集合稱謂）","s":"The local community center organizes weekly health screenings and free digital workshops specifically designed for the elderly.","t":"當地的社區中心每週舉辦專門為銀髮長輩設計的健康檢查以及免費數位學習工作坊。"},{"w":"aged","p":"adj.","d":"very old, or having reached a specified age (pronounced /ˈeɪ.dʒɪd/ or /eɪdʒd/)","c":"年邁的；老年的；…歲的","s":"The doctor gently reminded the family that their aged grandfather required warm clothing and continuous medical attention in winter.","t":"醫生親切地提醒這家人，他們年邁的祖父在冬天需要保暖的衣物與持續的醫療照護。"},{"w":"ancient","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the very distant past, especially thousand of years ago","c":"古代的；古老的","s":"Many adventurous tourists travel to Egypt every year to marvel at the massive stone pyramids built by ancient civilizations.","t":"每年許多喜愛冒險的遊客前往埃及，讚嘆由古代文明所建造的宏偉石頭金字塔。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel through an unfamiliar area to discover what is there, or to investigate","c":"探索；探險；探究；研討","s":"Equipped with strong helmets and bright headlights, the experienced team entered the deep underground cavern to explore its hidden passages.","t":"配戴堅固的頭盔與明亮的頭燈，那支經驗豐富的隊伍進入深邃的地下洞穴以探索其隱藏的通道。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"the action of traveling in or through an unfamiliar area in order to learn about it","c":"探索；探險；探勘","s":"Modern technological advancements in satellite robotics have opened up exciting new frontiers for deep-space exploration across our solar system.","t":"衛星機器人領域的現代科技進展，為我們太陽系內的深空探索開創了令人振奮的嶄新前沿。"},{"w":"explorer","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels to unfamiliar places in order to discover what is there","c":"探險家；探勘者","s":"The fearless Arctic explorer documented his dangerous journey across frozen mountains in an inspiring daily diary.","t":"那位無畏的北極探險家在一本鼓舞人心的每日日記中，記錄了他穿越冰封山脈的危險旅程。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"fortune – owl","cards":[{"w":"fortune","p":"n.","d":"chance or luck as an external force affecting human affairs","c":"好運；幸運（不可數）","s":"I had the good fortune of receiving a scholarship to study in London.","t":"我有幸獲得獎學金前往倫敦留學。贏得這個獎項肯定會為我們全家帶來好運。"},{"w":"fortune","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of money or valuable assets","c":"鉅款；大筆財富（可數）","s":"The author managed to make a fortune by writing popular fantasy novels for teenagers.","t":"那位作家靠著為青少年寫暢銷奇幻小說發了大財／賺得鉅款。"},{"w":"fortune","p":"n.","d":"a person's destiny or future condition","c":"命運；命途（可數/不可數）","s":"While visiting the busy night market, Susan decided to have her fortune told by a famous palm reader.","t":"在逛熱鬧的夜市時，蘇珊決定請一位著名的手相師幫她算命。"},{"w":"fortunate","p":"adj.","d":"favored by or involving good luck; lucky","c":"幸運的；僥倖的","s":"We were extremely fortunate to find an open hotel room during the crowded festival.","t":"在擁擠的節日期間，我們極為幸運地找到了一間空的飯店房間。"},{"w":"misfortune","p":"n.","d":"bad luck, or an unfortunate event","c":"不幸；厄運；逆境","s":"He had the misfortune to lose his passport on the very first day of his trip.","t":"他非常不幸在旅行的第一天就弄丟了護照。"},{"w":"glory","p":"n.","d":"high renown or honor won by notable achievements, or magnificent beauty","c":"光榮；榮耀；壯麗","s":"The brave national athletes fought hard to win glory for their country in the Olympic Games.","t":"勇敢的國家運動員們奮力拚搏，在奧林匹克運動會上為國家贏得榮耀。"},{"w":"glorious","p":"adj.","d":"having or deserving fame; magnificent or delightful","c":"光榮的；輝煌的；極美好的","s":"The football team celebrated their glorious victory after winning the intense championship match.","t":"足球隊在贏得激烈的冠軍賽後慶祝他們光榮的勝利。"},{"w":"hire","p":"v.","d":"to employ someone for wages, or to pay for temporary use of something","c":"僱用；聘請；租用","s":"Because the local police were busy, the family decided to hire a private detective to solve the mystery.","t":"因為當地警方很忙，這家人決定聘請一名私家偵探來解開謎團。"},{"w":"hire","p":"n.","d":"a newly recruited employee, or the act of hiring","c":"新進人員；僱用（可數/不可數）","s":"The manager introduced each new hire to all company departments on Monday morning.","t":"經理在週一早晨向所有公司部門介紹了每一位新進人員。"},{"w":"horn","p":"n.","d":"a hard permanent pointed outgrowth on the head of cattle, sheep, or goats","c":"（牛、羊等動物的）角","s":"The aggressive bull lowered its head to display its sharp horns to the warning crowd.","t":"那隻具攻擊性的公牛低下頭，向示警的人群展示其鋒利的獸角。"},{"w":"horn","p":"n.","d":"an instrument sounding a warning in a vehicle, or a brass wind instrument","c":"（汽車）喇叭；號角","s":"The impatient taxi driver began to honk his car horn repeatedly to clear the crowded intersection.","t":"那名不耐煩的計程車司機開始連續按他的汽車喇叭，以清理擁擠的路口。"},{"w":"take the bull by the horns","p":"v.phr.","d":"to deal directly and bravely with a difficult or dangerous situation","c":"挺身面對困難；當機立斷","s":"Instead of running away from his heavy debts, Gary decided to take the bull by the horns and talk to his bank.","t":"蓋瑞沒有逃避沉重的債務，而是決定挺身面對困難，主動與他的銀行協商。"},{"w":"opposite","p":"adj.","d":"completely different in nature, direction, or meaning","c":"相反的；對立的","s":"Even though the two scientists analyzed the same data, they reached completely opposite conclusions.","t":"儘管這兩位科學家分析了相同的數據，他們卻得出了截然相反的結論。"},{"w":"opposite","p":"adj.","d":"facing or situated directly across from something","c":"對面的；正相對的","s":"There is a quiet coffee shop on the opposite side of the street where students like to study.","t":"在街道對面的一側有一家安靜的咖啡館，學生們喜歡在那裡讀書。"},{"w":"opposite","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that is totally different from or the reverse of another","c":"相反的人事物；對立面","s":"Many expected him to be nervous on stage, but his relaxed behavior was the exact opposite.","t":"許多人原本以為他在舞台上會緊張，但他輕鬆的表現卻是完全相反的對立面。"},{"w":"opposite","p":"prep./adv.","d":"in a position facing someone or something but on the other side","c":"在…對面；面對面地","s":"Mr. Davis lives opposite the modern train station, so commuting to work is very convenient.","t":"戴維斯先生就住在現代化火車站的正對面，因此通勤上班非常方便。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to arrange into a structured whole, or to put things into systematic order","c":"組織；籌劃；整理","s":"Kelly spent two hours to organize her class notes carefully before she started studying for the final exam.","t":"凱莉在開始為期末考溫習之前，花了兩個小時仔細整理她的課堂筆記。"},{"w":"organized","p":"adj.","d":"arranged in a neat, systematic way, or able to plan efficiently","c":"有條理的；井然有序的","s":"Jessica is a highly organized secretary who manages complicated meeting schedules without any errors.","t":"潔西卡是一位極有條理的秘書，處理複雜的會議行程從未出錯。"},{"w":"organization","p":"n.","d":"an organized body of people with a particular purpose, or systematic arrangement","c":"組織；機構；體制；條理性","s":"Linda works for an international non-profit organization that provides clean water to developing villages.","t":"琳達在一所為開發中村落提供乾淨飲用水的國際非營利組織／機構工作。"},{"w":"organizer","p":"n.","d":"a person who arranges an event, or a device/book used for scheduling","c":"主辦者；籌辦人；萬用記事本","s":"The event organizer announced that the outdoor music festival would be postponed due to the hurricane.","t":"活動主辦者宣布，由於颶風來襲，戶外音樂節將順延舉行。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"present or existing from the beginning; initial","c":"最初的；原先的","s":"Our original plan was to visit Japan in February, but heavy snow forced us to change it to March.","t":"我們最初的計畫是二月份去日本旅遊，但大雪迫使我們將行程改到了三月。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"created directly by a person and not copied; completely novel","c":"具原創性的；新穎獨特的","s":"The scientific experiment was based on an original idea that nobody in the laboratory had ever explored.","t":"這項科學實驗是基於一個實驗室裡前所未見的原創／新穎想法。"},{"w":"original","p":"n.","d":"an authentic work of art or document, not a copy","c":"原件；正本；原作","s":"I brought a photocopy to the office because the museum keeps the precious original in a safe vault.","t":"我帶了一份影本到辦公室，因為博物館將珍貴的原件／真跡存放在安全的保險庫中。"},{"w":"originality","p":"n.","d":"the ability to think independently and creatively; novelty","c":"獨創性；創意；新穎","s":"The judges praised the young architect's drawing because it showed remarkable originality and elegance.","t":"評審們讚賞這位年輕建築師的圖紙，因為它展現了非凡的獨創性與優雅。"},{"w":"oven","p":"n.","d":"an enclosed compartment used for baking, heating, or roasting food","c":"烤箱；烤爐","s":"The delicious smell of beef roasting slowly in the oven filled every corner of the house.","t":"在烤箱中慢慢烘烤的牛肉美味香氣瀰漫了屋子的每個角落。"},{"w":"owl","p":"n.","d":"a nocturnal bird of prey with large eyes, a facial disc, and silent flight","c":"貓頭鷹","s":"Because an owl is a nocturnal animal, it hunts small mice at night and sleeps during the day.","t":"因為貓頭鷹是夜行性動物，牠在夜間捕獵小老鼠，白天睡覺。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"pearl – skip","cards":[{"w":"pearl","p":"n.","d":"a hard, round, lustrous white or silvery gem formed inside the shell of an oyster","c":"珍珠（可數）","s":"Kevin bought an elegant pearl necklace for his mother on her fiftieth birthday.","t":"凱文在母親五十歲生日時為她買了一條優雅的珍珠項鍊。"},{"w":"Pearl Harbor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a major US naval base in Hawaii, attacked by Japanese military aircraft in 1941","c":"珍珠港","s":"During our summer vacation in Hawaii, my family visited the famous historical memorial at Pearl Harbor.","t":"在夏威夷的暑假期間，我們全家參觀了位於珍珠港的著名歷史紀念館。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to cause someone to do something through reasoning or argument","c":"說服；勸告（動詞）","s":"I tried to persuade Nigel to join our weekend camping trip, but he still preferred to stay home.","t":"我試圖說服奈傑爾加入我們的週末露營之旅，但他仍然偏好待在家裡。"},{"w":"persuade sb. out of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to talk someone out of doing something unwise or risky","c":"勸某人放棄／打消…念頭","s":"His close friends tried hard to persuade him out of quitting his stable job during the economic crisis.","t":"他的摯友們努力勸阻他在經濟危機期間打消辭去穩定工作的念頭。"},{"w":"persuasion","p":"n.","d":"the action or fact of persuading someone or of being persuaded","c":"說服；說服力（不可數）","s":"Because the proposal was very reasonable, it took very little persuasion to get the director's full approval.","t":"因為這項企劃非常合理，幾乎不需什麼說服就獲得了主管的完全認同。"},{"w":"persuasive","p":"adj.","d":"good at convincing someone to do or believe something through reasoning","c":"有說服力的；使人心服的","s":"The defense lawyer presented a highly persuasive argument that convinced everyone in the courtroom.","t":"辯護律師提出了一個極具說服力的論點，說服了法庭上的所有人。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"to cause someone to believe firmly in the truth of something","c":"使確信；使信服（動詞）","s":"The accused man tried his best to convince the judge of his complete innocence.","t":"被告男子竭盡全力使法官確信他是完全清白的。"},{"w":"pill","p":"n.","d":"a small round piece of solid medicine that you swallow with water","c":"藥丸；藥片（可數）","s":"The doctor instructed the patient to take one yellow pill twice daily after meals for a full week.","t":"醫生指示病人每天飯後服用一次黃色藥丸，連續服用一整週。"},{"w":"tablet","p":"n.","d":"a small flat compressed piece of medicine, or a flat slab used for writing","c":"藥片；平板電腦；刻寫銘板","s":"Whenever David suffers from a terrible headache, he takes one aspirin tablet with a large glass of warm water.","t":"每當大衛頭痛劇烈時，他會配上一大杯溫水吞服一顆阿斯匹靈藥片。"},{"w":"capsule","p":"n.","d":"a small soluble gelatin case enclosing a dose of medicine; a spacecraft compartment","c":"膠囊；太空艙；小盒（可數）","s":"Doctors often prescribe medicine in gelatin capsule form so that nutrients are absorbed quickly in the stomach.","t":"醫生常開立明膠膠囊形式的藥物，以便營養成分能在胃中迅速被吸收。"},{"w":"ribbon","p":"n.","d":"a long, narrow strip of silk or cloth used for tying or decorating","c":"緞帶；絲帶；色帶","s":"The city mayor was invited to cut the ribbon at the grand opening ceremony of the new library.","t":"市長受邀為新圖書館的盛大開幕典禮剪綵。"},{"w":"blue ribbon","p":"adj.phr.","d":"of the highest quality; first-prize or elite","c":"頭等的；第一名的；最高榮譽的","s":"Her delicious apple pie won the coveted blue ribbon at the county fair baking contest.","t":"她美味的蘋果派在郡博覽會烘焙大賽中榮獲了令人稱羨的第一名藍緞帶。"},{"w":"sauce","p":"n.","d":"a liquid or semi-liquid substance served with food to add flavor","c":"醬汁；調味醬（可數/不可數）","s":"Vincent chopped two fresh cloves of garlic and added them to the bubbling tomato sauce.","t":"文森切了兩瓣新鮮大蒜，並將它們加入滾沸的番茄醬汁中。"},{"w":"saucer","p":"n.","d":"a shallow dish, typically having a circular indentation, on which a teacup rests","c":"茶碟；茶托；淺碟","s":"The polite waiter placed the hot ceramic teacup carefully on a matching white saucer.","t":"那位有禮貌的服務生小心翼翼地將滾燙的陶瓷茶杯放在配套的白色茶托／茶碟上。"},{"w":"shepherd","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to take care of and guide sheep","c":"牧羊人；羊倌","s":"The dedicated mountain shepherd stayed awake with his sheep day and night to protect them from wild wolves.","t":"那名盡職的高山牧羊人日夜守候在羊群身邊，保護牠們不受野狼侵害。"},{"w":"shepherd","p":"v.","d":"to guide or direct someone carefully and tenderly in a particular direction","c":"引領；帶領；悉心護送","s":"The tour guide carefully shepherded the foreign tourists through the crowded and noisy market streets.","t":"導遊悉心引領外國遊客穿過擁擠且吵鬧的市集街道。"},{"w":"sink","p":"n.","d":"a fixed basin with a water supply and drain, used for washing dishes or hands","c":"洗碗槽；洗手台；水槽","s":"After finishing the family dinner, there was a huge pile of dirty dishes in the kitchen sink.","t":"全家吃完晚餐後，廚房洗碗槽裡有一大堆髒盤子。"},{"w":"sink","p":"v.","d":"to go down below the surface of liquid; to drop or fall","c":"下沉；沉沒；使下陷","s":"Tommy tossed a heavy round pebble into the deep pond and watched it quickly sink to the bottom.","t":"湯米將一顆沉重的圓卵石扔進深池塘中，看著它迅速沉入池底。"},{"w":"sink one's teeth into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become fully, passionately, and energetically involved in a task or project","c":"全神貫注投入於…；大展身手","s":"The ambitious new reporter was eagerly searching for an investigative news story he could really sink his teeth into.","t":"那位雄心勃勃的新進記者正急切地尋找一則能讓他真正全力以赴大展身手的調查新聞報導。"},{"w":"skip","p":"v.","d":"to omit or leave out; to fail to attend a class or meal","c":"略過；翹（課）；省略（餐）","s":"Because I woke up thirty minutes late this morning, I had to skip breakfast and run to school.","t":"因為我今天早晨晚起了三十分鐘，我不得不略過早餐並狂奔去學校。"},{"w":"skip","p":"v.","d":"to move along lightly, stepping from one foot to the other with a hop","c":"輕跳；蹦蹦跳跳；跳繩","s":"Children love to skip rope together on the school playground during their fifteen-minute recess break.","t":"孩童們喜歡在十五分鐘的課間休息時間在學校操場上一同跳繩。"},{"w":"skip","p":"n.","d":"a light, springy hopping step or movement","c":"輕跳；蹦跳（可數）","s":"The graceful dancer made an elegant skip across the puddle to avoid getting her shiny shoes wet.","t":"那位優雅的舞者輕巧地輕跳跨過水坑，以避免弄濕她光亮的鞋子。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"suicide – tangerine","cards":[{"w":"suicide","p":"n.","d":"the act of intentionally causing one's own death","c":"自殺；自殺行為（不可數）","s":"Tragically, many teenagers struggling with severe school bullying have committed suicide in recent years.","t":"令人痛心的是，近年來許多遭受嚴重校園霸凌的青少年自殺身亡。"},{"w":"commit suicide","p":"v.phr.","d":"to intentionally end one's own life","c":"自殺；尋短（動詞片語）","s":"After losing all his investments in the stock market crash, the desperate man threatened to commit suicide.","t":"在股市崩盤中失去所有投資後，這名絕望的男子揚言要自殺。"},{"w":"survey","p":"n.","d":"an investigation of the opinions or experiences of a group of people based on a series of questions","c":"民意調查；調查研究（可數）","s":"A recent survey shows that the vast majority of citizens are satisfied with the national healthcare system.","t":"最近一項調查顯示，絕大多數公民對全民健保體系感到滿意。"},{"w":"survey","p":"v.","d":"to question a group of people in order to collect information; to examine an area carefully","c":"調查（民意）；審視；勘察（動詞）","s":"Over one thousand local television viewers were surveyed to better understand which entertainment programs they preferred watching.","t":"超過一千名當地電視觀眾接受了調查，以便更清楚了解他們偏好收看哪些娛樂節目。"},{"w":"suspect","p":"v.","d":"to have an idea of the presence or truth of something without certain proof; to believe someone is guilty","c":"懷疑；猜想；疑有（動詞，重音在後 /səˈspekt/）","s":"The strict high school teacher suspected the dishonest student of cheating on the chemistry final exam.","t":"那位嚴格的高中老師懷疑那個不誠實的學生在化學期末考作弊。"},{"w":"suspect","p":"n.","d":"a person thought to be guilty of a crime or offense","c":"嫌疑犯；犯罪嫌疑人（名詞，重音在前 /ˈsʌs.pekt/）","s":"The wealthy businessman immediately became the prime suspect after his business partner was mysteriously murdered.","t":"在商業合夥人被神秘謀殺後，那位富商立即成為了頭號嫌犯。"},{"w":"suspect","p":"adj.","d":"not to be relied on or trusted; possibly dangerous or false","c":"可疑的；不可靠的；有問題的（形容詞，/ˈsʌs.pekt/）","s":"His nervous and suspect actions in the luxury store immediately caught the sharp attention of the security guard.","t":"他在精品店中緊張且可疑的舉動立刻引起了警衛的敏銳注意。"},{"w":"suspicion","p":"n.","d":"a feeling or thought that something is possible, likely, or that someone is guilty","c":"懷疑；涉嫌；嫌疑（不可數/可數）","s":"Mrs. Watson had a strong suspicion that her noisy neighbor was secretly stealing fresh flowers from her garden.","t":"華生太太強烈懷疑她那吵鬧的鄰居在夜間偷偷摘取她花園裡的新鮮花朵。"},{"w":"suspicious","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing a cautious distrust of someone or something","c":"可疑的；多疑的；懷疑的","s":"The alert bank clerk became very suspicious of the nervous young man trying to withdraw a massive amount of cash.","t":"機警的銀行行員對那位試圖提領巨額現金且神情緊張的年輕人產生了極大懷疑。"},{"w":"doubt","p":"v.","d":"to feel uncertain about something or lack conviction","c":"懷疑；不相信；感到懷疑（動詞）","s":"Although the project seems very ambitious, no one can doubt her dedication to environmental protection.","t":"雖然這項企劃看似雄心勃勃，但無人能懷疑她對環境保護的奉獻精神。"},{"w":"doubt","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of uncertainty or lack of conviction","c":"懷疑；疑問；不確定（不可數/可數）","s":"Winning the international piano competition was without a doubt the greatest and proudest moment of her musical career.","t":"贏得國際鋼琴大賽毫無疑問是她音樂生涯中最偉大也最引以為傲的時刻。"},{"w":"swan","p":"n.","d":"a large waterbird with a long flexible neck, short legs, and typically all-white plumage","c":"天鵝（可數）","s":"In Hans Christian Andersen's beloved fairy tale, the bullied and awkward ugly duckling finally transformed into a graceful white swan.","t":"在安徒生備受喜愛的童話故事中，那隻飽受欺凌且笨拙的醜小鴨最終蛻變成為了一隻優雅的白天鵝。"},{"w":"swan song","p":"n.phr.","d":"the final performance, effort, or accomplishment given by an artist, athlete, or team before retirement or death","c":"告別演出；最後絕唱；退隱作","s":"Tonight's breathtaking and emotional ballet performance at the national theater was the aging ballerina's official swan song.","t":"今晚在國家劇院舉行令人驚嘆且感人肺腑的芭蕾舞演出，是這位年長芭蕾舞者的正式告別作／最後絕唱。"},{"w":"tangerine","p":"n.","d":"a small, sweet citrus fruit with a loose orange skin that peels easily","c":"橘子；椪柑；柑橘（可數）","s":"My grandmother kindly peeled a sweet and juicy tangerine and shared the delicious slices with the excited children.","t":"我祖母慈祥地剝開一顆酸甜多汁的椪柑／橘子，將美味的果瓣分給興奮的孩子們享用。"}]}];
